      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Nvidia CEO Affair Fallout: Binance NVDAUSDT Drops 4.2% vs Last US Close, Volume and Open Interest Rank No. 1 Among Top 8 Platforms Binance Research said management-related uncertainty at Nvidia emerged over the weekend. With US stocks closed, Binance’s NVDAUSDT perpetual contract briefly traded 4.2% below Nvidia’s previous US close. Over the past 24 hours, Binance’s Nvidia perpetual recorded $360.35 million in volume and $90.57 million in open interest, ranking first in both among the top eight platforms it tracks, accounting for 44% and 30.1% respectively. Earlier, Jensen Huang admitted being unfaithful to his wife and apologized. The person involved is reportedly Alice Huang, an executive at Megaspeed. Nvidia’s board launched an independent investigation the same day but said there is currently no evidence that national security or company secrets were compromised, and Huang will continue to serve as CEO. — link",
